            </a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">At least six metres from every building, exhaust pointed away, fully outdoors on all four sides.</strong> Not a garage with the door open, not under a porch or deck, not tight against a wall, and never under a tarp.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Walk the wall before you choose the spot and identify every window, vent and air intake, then account for the wind and re-check it as the weather shifts. Apply the same distance to your neighbour's house as to your own.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Put battery CO alarms on every sleeping level and test them before storm season. Then decide your generator's position today, on a dry afternoon, and mark it — so the decision is never made at midnight in the rain.
          </p>
